within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.N_NervousSystem.N01A_AnestheticsGeneral.N01AX10_Propofol;
model Propofol_Su2022_PD_tpr
  "sigmoid_emax exposure-response sweep — Su_2022 :: TPR (Total peripheral resistance)"
  extends Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep(
    E0 = 0.018,      // [mm Hg ml À1 min]
    Emax = -0.85,  // [mm Hg ml À1 min]
    EC50 = 2.96,  // [kg/m3; mg ml À1 × 1]
    gamma = 1.76,
    exposure_per_s = 1);   // 1 mg ml À1 per second
  // imax_as_negative_emax: Imax (Q323) enters SigmoidEmaxSweep as −Emax
  annotation(experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 30, Interval = 0.06),
    Documentation(info = "<html><body><h4>Propofol_Su2022_PD_tpr</h4><p>The steady-state exposure-response curve of Su H et al., <i>British journal of anaesthesia 128(5):806–816</i> 2022 (<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bja.2022.01.022\">doi:10.1016/j.bja.2022.01.022</a>) — Total peripheral resistance [mm Hg ml À1 min] against propofol mg ml À1 — obtained by sweeping the driver instead of simulating a dose. Model family: sigmoid_emax.</p><h4>The parameters, in the paper's terms</h4><pre>  E0    =      0.018 mm Hg ml À1 min drug-free response (baseline) (Base TPR, Q324)
  Emax  =      -0.85 mm Hg ml À1 min maximal effect term (E max_TPR, Q323)
  EC50  =       2.96 mg ml À1 exposure at half of the maximal effect term (EC 50 TPR, Q321)
  gamma =       1.76          Hill coefficient (g, Q325)</pre><p>The algebra is <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep\">SigmoidEmaxSweep</a>; this model only supplies the numbers. The x axis is one mg ml À1 of propofol per second of simulated time (exposure is in kg/m3): there is no state, no dose and no kinetics — plot <code>response</code> against <code>exposure</code> (or <code>time</code>).</p><h4>What it reproduces</h4><pre>  exposure = 0         response 0.018   (drug-free)
  exposure = EC50 (2.96 mg ml À1)  response -0.407
  exposure -> infinity  response -0.832</pre></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Su_2022: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: curated candidate</li></ul></body></html>"));
end Propofol_Su2022_PD_tpr;
